-- title:
--   Avg Over Distinct Bad Mass Le H BConsistency Error Of Line Point Bounds
-- statement:
--   **Distinct-tuple bad mass is bounded by the H-B consistency error.**
--
--   Let `params`, `strategy`, and `family` satisfy the field and strategy hypotheses, let $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta\ge0$, let $0<d$, and let $k\in\mathbb{N}$. If the line-point bound holds for every index below $k$, then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{avgOver}_{u\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\operatorname{Point}(\mathrm{params}))}\operatorname{avgOver}_{xs\sim\operatorname{distinctTupleDistribution}(\mathrm{params},k)}\operatorname{hBConsistencyBadMass}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{strategy},\mathrm{family},u,xs)\le\operatorname{hBConsistencyError}(\mathrm{params},\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta,k).
--   $$
--
--   The displayed error is
--
--   $$
--   44k^2m\left(\varepsilon^{1/32}+\delta^{1/32}+\gamma^{1/32}+\zeta^{1/32}+\left(\frac{d}{q}\right)^{1/32}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The proof replaces distinct-tuple averaging by uniform averaging, pays the total-variation loss, and applies the preceding coordinate estimate.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.avgOver_distinct_badMass_le_hBConsistencyError_ofLinePointBounds`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
